usage: plan.py unit [-h] [--plans-root PLANS_ROOT] [--title TITLE]
                    [--json JSON | --file FILE]
                    [--agent PROVIDER/MODEL[/EFFORT]] [--notes NOTES]
                    [--changed PATH] [--minutes MINUTES]
                    [--executed-by PROVIDER/MODEL[/EFFORT]] [--attempt-id ID]
                    [--evidence V1=PATH] [--actor ACTOR]
                    plan item add|next|U#
                    [context|dispatch|return|accept|rework|reject]

split an item into units and move them: add | <U#>
dispatch|return|accept|rework|reject

positional arguments:
  plan                  plan id, PLAN<N> or path
  item
  add|next|U#
  context|dispatch|return|accept|rework|reject

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --plans-root PLANS_ROOT
                        plans/ directory (default: nearest up from cwd)
  --title TITLE         add: unit title
  --json JSON           JSON text, or @file
  --file FILE           file holding the JSON
  --agent PROVIDER/MODEL[/EFFORT]
                        dispatch: the worker
  --notes NOTES
  --changed PATH        return: a changed path (repeatable)
  --minutes MINUTES
  --executed-by PROVIDER/MODEL[/EFFORT]
                        return: who did the work when not the dispatched
                        worker; route-checked
  --attempt-id ID       return|accept: registration attempt; a repeat is a no-
                        op
  --evidence V1=PATH    accept: check-evidence file of the unit (Task field
                        contract; see `plan.py schema check-evidence`;
                        repeatable)
  --actor ACTOR         PROVIDER/MODEL[/EFFORT] (default: the item executor,
                        else plan authoring)
